00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:25.000
The official synopsis reads "Four crew
members of an ice cap polar base

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:30.040
Ashley Carter, Bellows, Professor Albert
and Shona are under attack from the alien

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:31.130
Kantrofarri.

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:34.910
Fortunately for them help is on the way.
But desperate though their situation is,

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:39.020
how willing will they be to accept one
rescuer who arrives in a police box

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:42.370
and another who turns up on a sleigh
pulled by flying reindeer."

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:46.020
And then there's the quote listed "It's
Christmas Day, it's the North Pole,

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:49.350
and you're dying. Who you gonna call?" So these obviously

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:54.290
are the Kantrofarri. The real question is
is why does the Doctor need Clara's help?

00:00:54.290 --> 00:00:57.530
It does seem like a very the Doctor
saves Christmas with the help of Santa

00:00:57.530 --> 00:00:58.059
Claus

00:00:58.059 --> 00:01:02.410
and Clara. So Steven Moffat wrote the special. He called it "Scary, tense

00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:06.229
and claustrophobic. The Thing meets
Miracle on 34th Street.

00:01:06.229 --> 00:01:09.240
It's certainly the strangest bloody
thing I've ever written."

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:12.790
So that gives you an idea. It's going to be a really weird tale about digging things out of the ice,

00:01:12.790 --> 00:01:16.979
the aliens, and getting people to believe
in Santa Claus, like the idea of the myth

00:01:16.979 --> 00:01:20.750
of Santa Claus. They did that with Robin
Hood earlier this year, you know, is he real,

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:25.360
is he not real? Is the Doctor real, is he not real as seen from Clara's perspective.

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:28.549
Obviously the Doctor believes he's real but
I always loved that moment, there was that moment in

00:01:28.549 --> 00:01:30.439
Robin Hood where he wasn't quite sure.

00:01:30.439 --> 00:01:34.640
Santa is the one that actually came for
Clara first, the Doctor swooped in later.

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:37.960
This is a better shot of that base at the
North Pole. I'll be interested to see how

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:41.000
they deal with the myth about Santa's
workshop being at the North Pole,

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:44.119
if they try to integrate that into this
North Pole base because it seems like

00:01:44.119 --> 00:01:44.990
the team that's there

00:01:44.990 --> 00:01:48.220
has nothing to do with Santa. It's
hard to tell from this shot but the

00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:50.790
Kantrofarri actually look like they're
wearing uniforms

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:54.250
so either they're converted people or they got
dug out of the ice

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:58.860
and they've just been dethawing. Note to self, if you ever find an alien spacecraft buried in

00:01:58.860 --> 00:01:59.540
the ice

00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:02.661
do not dig it up or any aliens for that
matter.

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:06.130
We do have the names of the main cast
members, the official character names.

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:09.860
Nick Frost we know is Santa Claus, obviously. Michael Troughton, the son of the second

00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:11.760
Doctor is Professor Albert.

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:14.640
Maureen Beattie is Bellows. Faye Marsay

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:18.660
is Shona. Natalie Gumede is Ashley Carter. Nathan McMullen

00:02:18.670 --> 00:02:23.280
is Wolf and Dan Starkey, obviously, is Ian.
But they're the main cast so I would

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:27.260
assume anyone else that does not appear on this
cast list and is secondary character

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:31.700
is redshirt status. But usually Moffat picks
someone off pretty quickly.

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:35.390
To be fair the aliens would not be a
threat if someone didn't die right away.

00:02:35.390 --> 00:02:38.769
I just love this shot of Nick Frost
and Strax just swaggering in,

00:02:38.769 --> 00:02:42.550
just a giant gaping hole in the side of
the research base, no big deal.

00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:46.150
Just Santa Claus and his elves. It is so
bizarre seeing Dan Starkey without his

00:02:46.150 --> 00:02:46.989
makeup on.

00:02:46.989 --> 00:02:51.090
So Clara and the blackboard here, "You are dying." It could be foreshadowing for her

00:02:51.090 --> 00:02:52.989
or for the people at the research base.

00:02:52.989 --> 00:02:56.880
Santa implied that her belief in him was
actually a really big deal so that

00:02:56.880 --> 00:03:00.519
somehow might be tied to her survival. Here's
actually a much better shot of the

00:03:00.519 --> 00:03:01.560
Kantrofarri

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:05.310
standing up. it almost looks like you can
see the skin of a human neck underneath that

00:03:05.310 --> 00:03:06.170
giant head.

00:03:06.170 --> 00:03:09.910
So it's possible that the Kantrofarri are
converting people at the research base.

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:14.280
So just to address Clara Oswald. Steven
Moffat did say that they would address

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:17.489
what happened in Death in Heaven,
like the death of Danny and her leaving

00:03:17.489 --> 00:03:18.390
the Doctor

00:03:18.390 --> 00:03:21.400
like it would be part of the episode,
like a big part of the story. Jenna

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:24.390
Coleman has been back and forth about
whether or not she's leaving.

00:03:24.390 --> 00:03:28.010
Right now it looks like she's going to
stay on for at least 4 or 5 episodes of

00:03:28.010 --> 00:03:28.880
Series 9.

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:33.000
Peter Capaldi has been reported as
signing on for Series 9 and 10.

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:36.750
I've only seen that from one news
